      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single 5000 mg dose is also above the normal maximum single dose of 1000 mg. At 15 g/day, the risk of acute hepatotoxicity and liver failure is high, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n\nIf you do want 5000 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give your clinical rationale. I would still want to flag it before entering it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
